#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:197"
msgid ""
"Thou hast received a \n"
"good price for that!"
msgstr ""
"Has recibido un\n"
"buen precio por eso"

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:201"
msgid ""
"I suppose that I can part \n"
"with it."
msgstr ""
"Supongo que puedo \n"
"separarme de eso."

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:202"
msgid ""
"Alright, but not for\n"
"a penny less!"
msgstr ""
"De acuerdo, pero ni\n"
" un centavo menos!"

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:204"
msgid ""
"I shall not sell it \n"
"for anything less."
msgstr ""
"No lo venderé \n"
"por nada menos. "

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:205"
msgid ""
"Thou dost not have \n"
"enough money!"
msgstr ""
"¡No tienes \n"
"suficiente dinero! "

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:217"
msgid ""
"Lamp oil? Rope? Bombs? Dost\n"
"thou want it? It is thine my\n"
"friend, so long as thou\n"
"havest enough rubies!"
msgstr ""

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:220"
msgid ""
"They say cursed items often\n"
"do the opposite of what\n"
"they were meant to do."
msgstr ""
"Dicen que los objetos malditos\n"
"tienden a hacer lo contrario de \n"
"lo que se espera que hagan.."

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:222"
msgid ""
"Weapons come at different\n"
"levels of effectiveness. Wood\n"
"and bronze are weak, but steel\n"
"is very strong."
msgstr ""
"Las armas poseen diferentes \n"
"niveles de efectividad. Madera\n"
"y bronce son endebles pero el acero\n"
"es muy fuerte."

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:224"
msgid ""
"Beware of picture books. I\n"
"knew someone who touched one:\n"
"thenext thing they knew, they\n"
"were all alone on a tiny island."
msgstr ""
"Cuidáos de los libros ilustrados.\n"
"Conocí a alguien que tocó uno:\n"
"Lo siguiente que se supo, es que\n"
"estaba solo en una isla diminuta."

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:226"
msgid ""
"Goblins make good scavengers.\n"
"Do not leave powerful items\n"
"where they might find them!"
msgstr ""
"Los trasgos son grandes saqueadores.\n"
"No dejéis objetos poderosos\n"
"donde puedan encontrarlos!"

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:229"
msgid ""
"Thou canst bind wounds\n"
"with towels."
msgstr ""
"No podéis vendar una herida\n"
"con toallas."

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:230"
msgid ""
"Art thou hungry? Rat meat \n"
"is a staple down here."
msgstr ""
"¿Estáis hambriento? La carne de rata\n"
"es un alimento básico por estos lares."

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:232"
msgid ""
"They say Succubi enjoy trying\n"
"to steal mens' clothes."
msgstr ""
"Dicen que las súcubos se divierten\n"
"tratando de despojar a los hombres de su ropa."

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:233"
msgid ""
"The older food is, the more\n"
"likely it is to make one\n"
"sick when eaten."
msgstr ""
"Cuanto más pasada esté la comida, más\n"
"probable es que enfermes al comerla."

#. Versiones: 3.3.7
msgctxt "lang/en.txt:234"
msgid ""
"Mirrors can do odd\n"
"things at times."
msgstr ""
"En ocasiones los espejos\n"
"hacen cosas raras."

